ation epic. Per the docs-authoring priority exception, this edge does not push E002's P2 upstream — E001's P1 comes from HLR-1/HLR-2. |\n43\t\n44\tNo other edges:\n45\t\n46\t- No Investigation epics — the strategy states there are no open questions and\n47\t  the audit report enumerates the exact defects per flow (Step 3 decision rule:\n48\t  no unknown changes which epics exist or what they do).\n49\t- No onboarding chain — the Dashboard is an existing, Konflux-onboarded\n50\t  component per `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`,\n51\t  so no `repo-onboarding`, `license-validation`, or `konflux-onboarding` epics\n52\t  (Rules 19-22 do not fire). Rule 25 \"build pipeline green\" AC is not required\n53\t  because no `konflux-onboarding` epic is in any dependency chain.\n54\t- HLR-1 and HLR-2 are implemented as one epic (see traceability below), so\n55\t  there are no Implementation → Implementation edges.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n58\t\n59\t| HLR | Priority | Epic | Notes |\n60\t|-----|----------|------|-------|\n61\t| HLR-1 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 | Keyboard operability of the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission). |\n62\t| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 (bundled) | Bundled with HLR-1: the focus-indicator remediation is carried out in the same sweep over the same four flows' UI surfaces (same modals, same controls, same audit defect list). A separate epic would force a second pass over every flow and cannot ship independent user value — the audit treats visible focus as part of keyboard operability of these surfaces. |\n63\t| HLR-3 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E002 | docs-authoring epic; priority derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Normal` → P2 per the docs-authoring priority exception. |\n64\t\n65\tAll three HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n66\t\n67\t## Health Warnings\n68\t\n69\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n70\t  Dependencies table, no Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then) section, and no\n71\t  Non-Functional Requirements section. Epic acceptance criteria were derived\n72\t  from the HLRs and the problem statement; team ownership was taken from the\n73\t  architecture context (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard).\n74\t- **Documentation team assumption**: no owner is stated for the Documentation\n75\t  component. E002 is assigned to RHOAI Docs with a mandatory technical review by\n76\t  the Dashboard engineering team (Rule 24 AC); confirm the owning team before\n77\t  scheduling.\n78\t- **E001 size above the ~2-week guideline (kept whole deliberately)**: the four\n79\t  audited flows' defect remediation is estimated at ~2-3 weeks as a single\n80\t  sweep. Splitting per flow would duplicate work — the defects (focus traps in\n81\t  modals, unreachable controls, inconsistent focus indicators) cluster in\n82\t  shared Dashboard surfaces (modal/focus-management patterns common to all four\n83\t  flows), so one sweep avoids fixing the same shared component four times.\n84\t  **Conditional re-split trigger**: re-split by flow if the audit defect list\n85\t  resolves to materially more work than enumerated (e.g., remediation of the\n86\t  first flow uncovers >30 additional defects) or if the epic passes the\n87\t  2-week mark with two or more flows not yet started.\n88\t- **Customer schedule pressure (non-blocking)**: two public-sector customers\n89\t  require the republished VPAT before renewal. The renewal dates are outside\n90\t  this strategy's control; the decomposition puts the docs epic last (Rule 11)\n91\t  because the VPAT must reflect the fixed state. If the renewal date is close,\n92\t  consider shipping an interim conformance statement — a scope decision for the\n93\t  strategy owner, not a DAG change.\n94\t\n95\t## Tiered Delivery\n96\t\n97\tNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing. Both epics are\n98\tinternal to the platform; E002 is strictly sequenced behind E001.\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac0bb6959e8fc573","agent_id":"a989a1b033eaffd3a","session_id":"ebedd0d9-b226-4e93-9723-2e0aa7ef8109","uuid":"ba77a96f-95bf-43b0-9de2-c63700c654e9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:24:36.267Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2ec182e2d99d478","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
