{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3f133dde11296dd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility remediation for four core Dashboard flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Keyboard accessibility remediation for four core Dashboard flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic remediates the keyboard accessibility defects found by the\n34\taccessibility audit in the four core Dashboard flows — project creation,\n35\tworkbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission — so that each\n36\tflow is fully operable with keyboard alone, with no focus traps, no unreachable\n37\tcontrols, and consistent visible focus indicators. The audit report enumerates\n38\tthe exact defects per flow; this epic clears that list. It delivers the\n39\tengineering half of the accessibility conformance strategy; the updated\n40\tconformance documentation (VPAT and accessibility statement) that reflects this\n41\tfixed state is tracked separately and must not be published before this work is\n42\tcomplete.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Remediate every defect enumerated in the accessibility audit for the four\n47\t  audited flows: project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, and\n48\t  pipeline run submission.\n49\t- Eliminate focus traps in the modals used by these flows (including focus\n50\t  loss on open/close) so keyboard users can enter, complete, and exit each\n51\t  modal.\n52\t- Make every control in the audited flows reachable and operable by keyboard.\n53\t- Apply consistent, visible focus indicators across the audited flows'\n54\t  controls, per HLR-2.\n55\t- Verify each flow end-to-end with keyboard-only walkthroughs (manual\n56\t  verification is part of this epic's engineering work).\n57\t- Keep existing Dashboard tests/CI passing; add regression coverage for the\n58\t  fixed keyboard behaviors where the repo's test conventions allow.\n59\t\n60\tOut of scope (per strategy): screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard\n61\tfixes require, and flows outside the four audited ones.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- Each of the four audited flows can be completed end-to-end using keyboard\n66\t  alone, verified by a manual keyboard-only walkthrough of each flow.\n67\t- No focus traps remain in the modals of the audited flows; focus behavior on\n68\t  modal open and close is correct in each affected modal.\n69\t- Every control in the audited flows is reachable and operable by keyboard —\n70\t  the audit's \"unreachable controls\" findings are all remediated.\n71\t- Focus indicators are visible and consistent across all controls in the\n72\t  audited flows.\n73\t- Every defect in the audit report's per-flow enumeration is fixed, or has an\n74\t  explicitly recorded disposition (fixed / waived with rationale) — no\n75\t  silently dropped findings.\n76\t- Existing Dashboard CI and tests pass with the changes.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard,\n81\t  with no focus traps or unreachable controls — this epic's primary scope.\n82\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n83\t  flows — bundled into this epic because the remediation is one sweep over the\n84\t  same four flows' shared UI surfaces and the same audit defect list; a\n85\t  separate epic would force a second pass over every flow.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac0bb6959e8fc573","agent_id":"a989a1b033eaffd3a","session_id":"ebedd0d9-b226-4e93-9723-2e0aa7ef8109","uuid":"1fb0736a-4852-4fe1-af15-e48c10d2aeb2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:24:39.604Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3f133dde11296dd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
